-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_outputpath.pcpp - Directive: @outputpath

  @outputpath "<path>"; sets the folder the build writes to (the generated
  C++, zig's folders, the program), in the main module only (BNF.md sec 2).
  It resolves once, as every path directive ($P: = the folder pcpp.exe is
  in), so the CLI and the editor build in the same place. pcpp -o wins over
  it; without either the folder is output. This file names output itself
  ($P:output): every build writes there, never into a subfolder of it.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_outputpath;

/*
  @@test
    kind run
    expect
    | built where the source says
    | [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  @@end
*/

@outputpath "$P:output";

begin
  println("built where the source says");
end.
